Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

## 1. Before/After Every Test in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each test
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Before/After All Tests in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task PlaceOrder_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 3. Once Before/After All Tests in the Assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start WireMock
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // stop WireMock
    }
}
```

## 4. Once for the Entire Test Session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task Migrate(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await DatabaseMigrator.ApplyAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await DatabaseMigrator.DestroyAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick Reference

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be |
|-------|-----------|----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance |
| Class (once) | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | **static** |
| Assembly (once) | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | **static** |
| Session (once) | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | **static** |

**Global cross-cutting variant:** `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (also `Class`/`Assembly`) runs for *every* test/class regardless of which class the hook lives in — handy for logging or diagnostics. The context parameter and `CancellationToken` are optional in all cases.
